{"book":24,"chapter":27,"context":{"chapter":27,"title":"Wear the Yoke of Babylon","summary":"Jeremiah wears a wooden yoke and sends a message to envoys from Edom, Moab, Ammon, Tyre and Sidon who are meeting in Jerusalem: God has given the lands to Nebuchadnezzar, so they should submit and live. He warns Zedekiah and the priests not to believe prophets who say the temple vessels will soon return.","background":"The envoys likely gathered around 594 BC to plan a revolt against Babylon. The KJV's verse 1 names Jehoiakim, but the chapter's own details (vv. 3, 12; 28:1) point to Zedekiah's reign, and some Hebrew manuscripts and early translations read 'Zedekiah' there.","customs":[{"term":"Bonds and yokes","verses":"27:2","note":"A wooden yoke bar strapped across an ox's neck. Wearing one in public made submission to Babylon impossible to ignore."}],"watchFor":["The Creator gives the earth 'unto whom it seemed meet unto me' (v. 5).","'Serve the king of Babylon, and live' (vv. 12, 17).","The great bronze pillars, sea and stands are named (v. 19); 2 Kings 25:13-17 tells their fate."],"connections":["Jeremiah 28:1","2 Kings 25:13-17","Daniel 2:37-38","Ezra 1:7"]},"verses":{"1":{"w":[["בְּרֵאשִׁית","bereshit","H7225","HR/Ncfsc","in [the] beginning of"],["מַמְלֶכֶת","mamlekhet","H4467","HNcfsc","[the] reign of"],["יְהוֹיָקִם","yehoyakim","H3079","HNpm","Jehoiakim"],["בֶּן","ben-","H1121","HNcmsc","[the] son of"],["יֹאושִׁיָּהוּ","yoshiyahu","H2977","HNpm","Josiah"],["מֶלֶךְ","melekh","H4428","HNcmsc","[the] king of"],["יְהוּדָה","yehudah","H3063","HNpl","Judah"],["הָיָה","hayah","H1961","HVqp3ms","it came"],["הַדָּבָר","hadavar","H1697","HTd/Ncmsa","the word"],["הַזֶּה","hazeh","H2088","HTd/Tm","<the> this"],["אֶל","'el-","H413","HR","to"],["יִרְמְיָה","yirmeyah","H3414","HNpm","Jeremiah"],["מֵאֵת","me'et","H854","HR/R","from with"],["יְהוָה","yahweh","H3068","HNpt","Yahweh"],["לֵאמֹר","lemor","H559","HR/Vqcc","<to> saying"]]},"2":{"w":[["כֹּה","koh-","H3541","HD","thus"],["